Bug 2063333 - Persist the real name of hashed-name folders in the summary at creation. r=tobyp

A folder whose name contains characters that can't be used in a filename
is stored on disk under a hashed name (NS_MsgHashIfNecessary), which
differs from its real name. Its real name was only ever kept in the
folder cache (via nsMsgLocalMailFolder::WriteToFolderCacheElem), never in
the folder's summary file: nothing calls SetFolderName() when a folder is
created since Bug 1960526 removed the SetPrettyName() call from the
creation flow. So once folderCache.json was missing or invalid (e.g.
after moving a profile), such a folder was displayed under its ugly
hashed on-disk name instead of its real name.

Fix this by persisting the folder's real name in the summary when the
folder is stored under a different (hashed) on-disk name: in both stores'
CreateFolder(), alongside SetMailboxName() (the on-disk name), also call
SetFolderName() with the real name. Special and ordinary folders are
unaffected, since for them the on-disk name equals the real name and the
folderName property stays empty as before.

Adds a regression test which creates a folder whose name contains an
illegal character and checks that its summary contains the real name.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318494


